MY PROJECTS (Full Technical Detail)
Project 1: Uber Ride-Booking Data Pipeline — Medallion Architecture

Tech Stack: Azure Event Hubs, ADF, Databricks, DLT, PySpark, Jinja2, Delta Lake
Type: Individual project, fully designed and built by me
Architecture:

Ingestion Layer (2 paths):

Real-time path: A small application sends ride-booking events to Azure Event Hubs in real-time
Batch path: A metadata-driven ADF pipeline copies historical ride data and mapping files from GitHub to ADLS Gen2

Processing Layer (Databricks, PySpark):

Bronze Layer: Raw data stored as-is — both batch files and streaming events ingested via Autoloader / readStream
Silver Layer: Data cleaning, schema enforcement, deduplication, combining historical + real-time rides, joining mapping/reference tables using reusable Jinja2 SQL templates (metadata-driven, configurable joins)
Gold Layer: Final analytics-ready tables — fact table (ride_fact) and dimension tables (rider_dim, driver_dim, location_dim, time_dim) following Star Schema design

Key Technical Decisions:

SCD Type 2 implemented on location_dim to track historical changes in location attributes
Jinja2 templating used to generate repeatable SQL joins — avoids hardcoded transformation logic
DLT (Delta Live Tables) used to unify batch and streaming with stateful watermarking
Databricks Jobs scheduled on 15-minute triggers for data freshness
Medallion Architecture ensures data quality improves at each layer
Project 2: Spotify Data Lakehouse — Incremental CDC & Governance

