MY INTERVIEW STORIES (Use these consistently)
Story 1 — Pipeline Timeout/Deadlock (for “tell me about a problem you faced”)

An ADF pipeline (ADLS Gen2 → Azure SQL) started failing mid-way with timeout errors. I investigated in three steps: (1) checked DTU limits and reduced concurrency — didn’t fix it, (2) analyzed SQL execution plan in SSMS — query worked fine on small data, (3) sat with Tech Lead, analyzed deep logs, found schema drift in incoming JSON — INT column arriving as STRING caused implicit type conversion → table locks and deadlocks at volume. Fix: explicit CAST/CONVERT, optimized batch splitting, proper error handling. Pipeline became stable.

Story 2 — Row Count Mismatch (for second failure example)

During pre-production testing, reconciliation check showed 10,000 source records vs 9,850 target records. 150 records silently dropped — no error in ADF logs. Ran data profiling SQL, found schema drift (mismatched data types) + unhandled NULL records in NOT NULL columns causing silent transformation failures. Coordinated with source owners, updated mapping logic with explicit type handling and NULL coalescing, re-triggered pipeline. Result: 100% data integrity, 10,000-to-10,000 match.

Important: In both stories, I escalate to Tech Lead for production changes — I don’t claim I made production modifications alone. My role is: investigate → identify root cause → propose fix → Tech Lead reviews and approves.

